      <h2 id="what-is-gamepad-tester">What is a gamepad tester?</h2>
      <p>Gamepad Tester is a free browser-based tool for checking whether a USB or Bluetooth controller is sending the inputs you expect. Connect the gamepad in Windows, macOS, or Linux first, then press a button to wake the browser Gamepad API. The live tester shows <a class="inline-link" href="/button-test/">buttons</a>, D-pad directions, analog sticks, trigger travel, <a class="inline-link" href="/stick-drift-test/">drift</a>, jitter, deadzone reference, circle coverage, <a class="inline-link" href="/vibration-test/">supported vibration</a>, and raw mapping data. It works with many Xbox, PlayStation, Switch, and generic PC controllers. Results describe the signal exposed by your browser, so they do not replace a hardware repair tool or firmware calibration utility — <a class="inline-link" href="/about/">read why this tool never writes to your controller</a>. If your controller is not detected, try USB, close Steam Input, and reload the page in desktop Chrome or Edge.</p>
